All three explicitly set the `this` context for a function. The difference is in HOW they invoke the function:

`.call(thisArg, arg1, arg2, ...)`: Calls the function immediately. Arguments passed individually.
greet.call(user, 'Hello', '!');

`.apply(thisArg, [arg1, arg2])`: Calls the function immediately. Arguments passed as an array (useful when you have an array of args).
greet.apply(user, ['Hello', '!']);
Math.max.apply(null, [1, 5, 3]);  // classic use case

`.bind(thisArg, ...partialArgs)`: Does NOT call the function. Returns a NEW function with `this` permanently bound. Arguments can be partially applied.
const boundFn = greet.bind(user, 'Hello');
boundFn('!');  // called later with pre-bound context

