The N+1 problem occurs when you fetch N records, then make N additional queries to fetch related data for each record:

// BAD: 1 query for courses + N queries for instructor (N+1 total)
const courses = await db.query('SELECT * FROM courses LIMIT 10');
for (const course of courses) {
  course.instructor = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [course.instructor_id]);
}

Fixes:
1. JOIN query: Get everything in one query
SELECT c.*, u.name as instructor_name
FROM courses c JOIN users u ON c.instructor_id = u.id LIMIT 10;

2. Eager loading (ORMs like Prisma):
const courses = await prisma.courses.findMany({
  include: { instructor: true }
});

3. DataLoader (for GraphQL) — batch all individual IDs into one WHERE IN query.

